{"content":"# gh-850 latch VOID — voids a VALID latch on probe degradation

⚠️ **IMPORTANT**

`vProbe.green === false` does not distinguish "no completed-green dispatched run on this head" from "the probe failed". Both `hasSuccessfulDispatchedRun` and `PROBE_WORKER_SOURCE` **fail OPEN** — their catch branches warn and return `green: false` — and the probe shape `{active, verdict, green, newest}` exposes no degraded/error flag.

So a transient `gh api` failure (rate limit, network blip) on a head that IS covered by a completed-green dispatched run passes this condition, and the block **strips a valid `ai_validated` latch** and re-dispatches — violating AC2's economy exactly on the failure path, once per transient error (self-heals only via the re-latch on the next green, after a wasted CI run). This is the destructively-acting-on-uncertain-evidence pattern the sibling guards avoid: the gh-842 guard comment states the convention explicitly — "a probe degradation keeps the legacy skip (retry next tick)".

**Suggested fix** — give the probe a degradation signal and refuse to void on it:

```javascript
// in PROBE_WORKER_SOURCE catch branch + the four helper catch branches:
// out.degraded = true (or return {degraded:true} from the helpers)
...
if ((ticket.labels || []).indexOf('ai_validated') !== -1 &&
    vProbe && !vProbe.green) {
    if (vProbe.degraded) {
        console.log('  ⏭️  ' + key + ' cover probe degraded — latch kept, retry next tick');
        continue;
    }
    // ...the strip
}
```

If plumbing a `degraded` flag through all five probe paths is too invasive for this PR, an acceptable minimal mitigation is to only strip when the probe positively returned a run list (e.g. expose `newest`/list length even when green is false) — but the current shape cannot tell the two cases apart at all.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment2.md"}

{"content":"# gh-850 latch VOID — real label write under DRY

💡 **SUGGESTION**

`github_remove_label` here is not guarded by `if (!DRY)`, unlike every other mutating call in this same action: the `validation_failed` park-clear above (`if (!DRY)` ~line 1936), the park comment (`!alreadyParked && !DRY` ~line 2182), and `dispatchCiWorkflow`, which exists precisely because of a live bug — "a DRY SM tick really dispatched CI … DRY means NO side effects" (fa 2026-09-27). DRY ticks do execute `validate_pr` actions (they reach `dispatchCiWorkflow`), so a dry tick on a latched PR with a bare head would really strip `ai_validated`.

```javascript
if (!DRY) {
    try {
        github_remove_label({ ... });
    } catch (eLatchVoid) { ... }
}
```

Note the pre-existing latch-skip arm's `github_add_labels` a few lines above has the same gap, so this is consistency-with-surrounding-code rather than a new class of bug — worth fixing both while here.
